  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Administration of Equity Investment Glacierwater Pte. Ltd. in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The transaction involves the administration by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) of an equity investment of $4,000,000, with an initial investment of $1,000,000 in Glacierwater Pte. Ltd., a holding company in Singapore, to expand its operations in Bangladesh (through its operating Bangladesh subsidiary, Tiger New Energy Co. Ltd., collectively the &amp;quot;Company&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Tiger&amp;quot;). The investment is to be provided by the ADB Ventures Investment Fund 1 under the ADB Ventures Financing Partnership Facility. The balance of the approved amount may be invested as equity or quasi-equity in subsequent fundraising rounds that Tiger is expected to undertake. Consistent with the established fund documents, ADB will not invest its own capital alongside the fund.</narrative>
  </description>
